  "visualBrief": "River château with five actual gallery arch voids, independent old-mill boat passage, pointed chapel glazing and polygonal study. Nine gallery windows/oculus dormers per long face, pale limestone and steep slate roof, cutwaters and upper lookouts. Three-bay north entrance with supported open balcony, crossed mullions, elaborate original dormer relief, four conical corner turrets, tall chimneys and open clock lantern. Detached corbelled Marques Tower with conical roof, stair turret, divided dormer, chimney and open cupola; immediate retaining terrace and arched entry bridge. Separate gardens, service houses, interiors, people and photographic textures excluded.",
